Treasury::depositEth
├ when contract is paused
│ └ it reverts
├ when caller does not have Depositor role
│ └ it reverts
└ when contract is not paused and caller has Depositor role
    └ it deposits Ether and emits TreasuryDeposit event

Treasury::withdrawEth
├ when contract is paused
│ └ it reverts
├ when caller does not have WithdrawalAuthority role
│ └ it reverts
├ when to address is null
│ └ it reverts with ZeroAddress
├ when feeReceiver address is null
│ └ it reverts with ZeroAddress
├ when withdrawal amount exceeds contract balance
│ └ it reverts with InsufficientFunds
└ when contract is not paused and caller has WithdrawalAuthority role and all parameters are valid
    └ it transfers the correct amount to `to` and fee to `feeReceiver` and emits TreasuryWithdrawal event

Treasury::emergencyWithdraw
├ when caller does not have Emergency role
│ └ it reverts
├ when withdrawal amount exceeds contract balance
│ └ it reverts with InsufficientFunds
└ when caller has Emergency role and withdrawal amount is valid
    └ it transfers the correct amount to caller and emits EmergencyTreasuryWithdraw event

Treasury::pause
├ when caller does not have Pauser role
│ └ it reverts
└ when caller has Pauser role
    └ it pauses the contract

Treasury::unpause
├ when caller does not have Starter role
│ └ it reverts
└ when caller has Starter role
    └ it unpauses the contract

Treasury::reinitialize
├ when contract is already initialized
│ └ it reverts
└ when contract is not initialized
    └ it grants roles to oldOwner


